  "whyItMatters": "Under axial compression a frame that sways (P-Delta) and members that bow (P-delta) pick up additional moments and displacements that a first-order analysis does not see. Where the amplification is material the first-order results are unconservative: smaller drift, smaller column and beam moments. AISC 360-22 C1 requires second-order effects to be considered in the required strengths.",
